---
import Case from "../../layouts/Case.astro";

const work = [
  {
    title: "HR system → Microsoft 365 profile sync",
    text: "A daily .NET background service that copies employee data from Workday into Microsoft 365 profiles: a field-mapping screen for admins, change detection so only changed records are written, retries with backoff, and a run history.",
    tags: ".NET · Microsoft Graph · Workday API",
    demo: { href: "/lab/#sync-pilot", label: "Public rebuild: SyncPilot" },
  },
  {
    title: "Notifications for a ticketing product",
    text: "Email and in-app notifications in real time, built so that one event never produces duplicate alerts. Part of the 102 pull requests merged in 51 days, alongside a knowledge base, reply templates and message moderation.",
    tags: ".NET 10 · SignalR · Microsoft Graph",
  },
  {
    title: "AI ticket translation in 5 languages",
    text: "Tickets are translated for agents with the customer's text kept apart from the instructions, so a ticket cannot steer the model.",
    tags: "LLM · .NET · Vue",
    demo: { href: "/lab/#inbox-triage", label: "Public rebuild: InboxTriage" },
  },
  {
    title: "A product extension for a Nordic bank, built solo",
    text: "Navigation tree and a continuous reader for a large handbook, from an empty repository to delivery: batched background loading, scroll sync between tree and reader, and localization.",
    tags: "TypeScript · Vue · .NET",
  },
  {
    title: "Connectors to enterprise systems",
    text: "Integrations shipped with Workday, ServiceNow, SAP SuccessFactors, Adobe Acrobat Sign, Microsoft Graph and SharePoint, each with change detection and retries.",
    tags: "REST · OAuth · background jobs",
  },
];
---

<Case
  slug="enterprise"
  title="Enterprise .NET and Vue work: 102 PRs in 51 days · Thuan Nguyen"
  description="Enterprise work on a Microsoft 365 intranet product for Nordic customers: 102 pull requests merged in 51 days, 37 codebases, integrations with Workday, ServiceNow, SAP SuccessFactors and Adobe Acrobat Sign. No client code or screens shown."
>
  <div class="prose intro">
    <h2>The outcome</h2>
    <p>
      Since 2024 I have built extensions and integrations for a Microsoft 365 intranet product used by enterprise
      and public-sector customers in the Nordics: banks, retail groups and cities. I have worked in 37 of its
      customer codebases. On one ticketing product, 102 of my pull requests were merged in 51 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      Client names, code and screens are confidential, so this page describes the work by type. Where a pattern
      is useful to show, I rebuilt it from scratch with sample data in the lab.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ol class="work">
    {
      work.map((w, i) => (
        <li>
          <span class="mono idx">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
          <div>
            <h3>{w.title}</h3>
            <p>{w.text}</p>
            <p class="mono tags">{w.tags}</p>
            {w.demo && <a href={w.demo.href}>{w.demo.label} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>}
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>How the work is done</h2>
    <p>
      Large tickets start as a short written plan that a reviewer can check before code exists. Claude Code drafts
      the change in an isolated branch; I run it, read every line, add tests where behaviour matters, and open the
      pull request under my name. That loop is what makes 102 merged pull requests in 51 days possible without
      lowering the bar of a team review.
    </p>

    <h2>What this means for your project</h2>
    <p>
      If your company runs on .NET, Vue or React and talks to HR, ticketing or document systems, I have most
      likely connected something similar before, and I know that the hard part is the retries, duplicates and
      permissions, not the first API call.
    </p>
  </div>
</Case>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .work {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 36px 0 8px;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .work li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 44px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 22px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .work li:first-child {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .idx {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--cobalt-ink);
    padding-top: 4px;
  }

  .work h3 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .work p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .work .tags {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .work a {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
</style>
